NAME
Streamlined Logistics

VERSION
0.10.25

SUMMARY (paste into the Brief Overview field)
All your storage in one window: link your chests, then see, search, take, store and use their items from anywhere. Favorites, a category tree, drag and drop, chests named for categories, Quick Deposit and one-click Re-Sort. Needs Kiln.

DESCRIPTION (Markdown, paste into the Detailed Description field)

[center][size=6][b][color=#e6a050]Streamlined Logistics[/color][/b][/size]

[i][color=#e6a050]Ever wanted to just… play the game, without having to deal with the Inventory Management minigame ? Now you can.[/color][/i][/center]

Streamlined Logistics is intended as an all-in-one storage mod for [b]Kiln[/b]. 

Press [b]F2[/b] and every chest you linked shows up as one searchable list next to your hotbars and backpack. Take what you need, drag it where you want it, store your loot, or let Quick Deposit and Re-Sort put everything into the right chests for you. Need a specific item ? Just open the menu : you favorited ones wait for you at the top, and everything else is searchable and neatly organized in tabs and categories.

If you fully set it up, you'll never have to worry about your inventory again so you can just focus on actually playing the game : set up quick auto deposit and salvage, auto-rename and have a few unnamed magic chests around and your inventory will get out of your way so you can focus on exploring and building. 

[hr]

[center][size=5][b]Features[/b][/size][/center]

[size=4][b]Control Center[/b][/size]

The F2 menu offers :

[list]
[*][b]Linked Chests[/b] on the left, your [b]Hotbars[/b] and [b]Inventory[/b] on the right, with every item totalled across all linked chests.
[*][b]Grid or list view[/b]. Gear is listed per level and rarity.
[*][b]Search[/b]: every word you type must be in the item's name, in any order. By default a search looks through every category, whatever tab is open ([b]Search Every Tab[/b], can be turned off).
[*][b]Category tree[/b] built from the game's own data and curated for the occasional straggler : Gear, Consumables, Placeables, Building, Other and Materials, each with sub-categories (Weapons, Shields, Armor, Cosmetics, Rings, Tools, Meals, Raw Food, Potions, Ammo, Spells, Stations, Furniture and more).
[*][b]Category tabs[/b] (All, Favorites, then each group), headers that fold and stay folded, and like items kept together (all tiers of one item side by side, all tools next to each other).
[*][b]Ungroup[/b] to see the content chest by chest instead of one merged list.
[*][b]Item details on hover[/b] : for any item you have looked at in the game's own screens this session, the tooltip shows the game's full item detail (damage, perks, gems, description). Other items show the rows of the game's own tooltip (food effects and duration, spell and tool costs) and their description, in your game language.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Moving Items[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Take and store with one click.[/b] RMB takes a stack from the chests or stores a stack from your backpack.
[*][b]Drag and drop[/b] with LMB between the two sides. Hold [b]Shift[/b] when you let go to move every stack of that item.
[*][b]Drop onto your hotbars[/b]: items go to hotbar 1, then hotbar 2, then your backpack. If all three are full, nothing moves.
[*]Drag between your hotbars and your inventory, too.
[*]Stored items go to the chest that already holds the most of them, otherwise the nearest one with room. Gear keeps its level and upgrades: every move is the game's own.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Use from Chests[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]MMB[/b] (or the Use button) uses a food, drink, potion, bandage or scroll exactly as from your hotbar: the animation plays and the buff shows in the buff panel with its real effects and duration.
[*]Works on items in chests (moved into your backpack first), in your backpack and on your hotbars.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Favorites[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Shift + RMB[/b] marks an item as a favorite, in the mod's window [b]and[/b] in the game's own inventory, chest and station screens. With a controller, press [b]L3[/b] on the selected slot.
[*]Favorites get a [b]gold border[/b] (in your inventory and in chest screens), are listed first, and [b]stay in your backpack[/b] when you use the game's Deposit All, Deposit Stacks or a Quick Stack Station.
[*][b]Gear favorites are per rarity[/b], so favoriting your Legendary staff doesn't protect the Uncommon copy you just picked up.
[*]The [b]Construction Hammer[/b], the [b]Summoning Staff[/b], and the [b]Overgrowth[/b] and [b]Decay[/b] tools can be favorited too, whatever they currently have selected.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Chest names that mean something[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Name a chest after a category ([i]Weapons[/i], [i]Meals[/i], [i]Ores[/i]) or a whole group ([i]Gear[/i], [i]Materials[/i]) and Quick Deposit and Re-Sort send it exactly that.
[*][b]Rename from the window[/b]: the name column is a dropdown of every category name. RMB on it to type a custom name instead. Names are the game's own, so they are saved with the world and everyone sees them.
[*][b]Specific before general[/b]: a chest named [i]Weapons[/i] fills before one named [i]Gear[/i]. When every chest of the best name is full, the next one takes over.
[*]Start a chest's name with [b]--[/b] and the mod never puts anything in it.
[*][b]Auto-Name Chests[/b] (optional): when nothing has room for an item, the closest chest that still has its default name is named for it, either by sub-category ([i]Weapons[/i]) or by group ([i]Gear[/i]).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Quick Deposit[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Inside a base, press [b]Sort Inventory twice[/b] (G by default, or LT + X) or use a [b]Quick Stack Station[/b], and your backpack empties into the base's chests.
[*]The [b]Quick Deposit button[/b] in the window sends your backpack to your linked chests, wherever you are.
[*][b]Auto Quick Deposit[/b] (optional): when loot fills your backpack, a quick deposit runs by itself (at most every 10 seconds). Only looting triggers it, not taking from your own chests or crafting.
[*]Existing stacks are topped up first, then items go to a chest named for their category, then to a chest that already holds them.
[*]Never touched: your hotbars, what you wear, your favorites, chests named with [b]--[/b], and Magic Chests with Receive Quick Stacking turned off.
[*][b]Quick Deposit and Auto Salvage[/b]: set rules for Weapons, Shields, Armor and Rings, matching items get deposited, the rest remain in your inventory. Set up auto salvage and "the rest" can be salvaged when you loot it. (Note that it reaches your inventory first, so you still unlock recipes for items that you loot.)
[*]A [b]report[/b] tells you what went where and what stayed, including which chest name is missing ("No chest named Ores (Iron Ore, Copper Ore)").
[*]The chests that received items are [b]highlighted[/b] with the game's own outline, [b]visible through walls[/b].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Re-Sort Chests[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]One button moves every item sitting in the wrong linked chest into a linked chest whose name asks for it. Items no chest asks for stay where they are.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Categories overview[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Every category with a show/hide checkbox, how many of its items your linked chests hold, whether a chest is named for it (and how many), and how many free slots those chests have left.
[*][b]LMB on a category[/b] highlights every chest named for it in the world. LMB on a group highlights the group's chests and all of its sub-categories' chests.
[*]Materials and Building blocks are hidden by default, since you mostly use them through the crafting menu and the Construction Hammer. A search still finds them.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Settings in the window[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]A Settings tab with every option and an explanation on hover. Changes apply at once and are saved. The same settings are also on the mod's page in Kiln's menu.
[/list]

[hr]

[size=5][b]How to Use[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Getting started[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Load a world you host (single player counts) and press [b]F2[/b].
[*]Open the [b]Chests[/b] tab. Tick the chests you want, or press [b]Link Nearby Chests[/b] to link everything within the Link Radius (100 m by default). Linking moves nothing; it only adds the chest to the list.
[*]Go back to the [b]Items[/b] tab. Everything in your linked chests is now on the left, your hotbars and backpack on the right.
[/list]

Only Magic Chests are offered for linking by default. Turn on [b]Link Regular Chests[/b] in the Settings tab to link regular chests too.

[size=4][b]Controls in the window[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]LMB[/b] : select an item (its buttons appear above the list: Take Stack, Take All, Store, Use, Favorite)
[*][b]RMB[/b] : take a stack from the chests, or store a stack from your backpack
[*][b]Shift + RMB[/b] : mark or unmark a favorite
[*][b]MMB[/b]: use the item (food, drinks, potions, bandages, scrolls)
[*][b]Drag & Drop[/b] : move a stack to the other side. Hold [b]Shift[/b] when you release to move every stack. Drop on the Hotbars list to fill hotbar 1, then 2, then the backpack.
[*][b]Hover[/b] : item details and which chests hold it
[*][b]Escape[/b] or [b]F2[/b] : close the window
[/list]

[size=4][b]Controls in the game's own screens[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Shift + RMB[/b] on a slot (or [b]L3[/b] on the selected slot with a controller) marks or unmarks its item as a favorite.
[*][b]Sort Inventory twice[/b] (G G) inside a base: Quick Deposit.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Setting up sorted storage[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]In the [b]Chests[/b] tab, pick a category name from each chest's name dropdown ([i]Weapons[/i], [i]Meals[/i], [i]Ores[/i]...). Use the [b]Show[/b] button to see which chest is which in the world.
[*]Open the [b]Categories[/b] tab to check which categories have a chest and how much room is left. LMB a category to light up its chests.
[*]Press [b]Re-Sort Chests[/b] once to move what you already own into the right chests.
[*]From then on, [b]G G[/b] in your base, or the Quick Deposit button anywhere, keeps it sorted. Turn on [b]Auto Quick Deposit[/b] and it happens on its own whenever loot fills your backpack.
[/list]

Tip : turn on [b]Auto-Name Chests[/b] in the Settings tab and drop a few unnamed chests in your base. The mod names them as it needs them.

[size=4][b]Changing the key[/b][/size]

The key is [b]Open Streamlined Logistics[/b] in the Keys tab of Kiln's menu.

[hr]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln]Kiln[/url] mod loader, [b]0.2.0-dev.30.5 or newer[/b].
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Add the archive through Kiln.
[*]Start the game. The mod shows up in Kiln's Mods page. It has its own settings menu inside its F2 menu, so you don't have to go through Kiln for that.
[/list]

To update, check with Kiln or download the newest version and install it manually.

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Works in a world you host[/b] (single player or as the host). Joining someone else's world and dedicated servers are not supported yet.
[*][b]XHL-Remote Chest[/b]: Streamlined Logistics replaces it and does not need XHL-Core. They don't share links. Running both is not recommended.
[*][b]Quick Deposit (Greeneye)[/b]: while it is installed and enabled, this mod's own G G deposit stands down and leaves it to Quick Deposit.
[*][b]Custom categories[/b]: if a [b]chestsort_categories.json[/b] sits next to the game's exe (the file Quick Deposit uses), the material categories are read from it and follow your edits live. Otherwise the copy bundled with the mod is used.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Links are stored by chest position and are not yet kept per world.
[*]The repair kit can't be used from the window; use it from your hotbar.
[*]The game's full item detail (damage, perks, gems) only shows for items you have looked at in the game's own screens this session.
[*]No controller button to open the window yet.
[*]A large Re-Sort takes a little while; the window's other buttons wait until it ends.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Planned features[/b][/size]

These are designed and waiting on a Kiln update that gives mods what they need. They will come as soon as Kiln supports them.

[list]
[*][b]Craft from your linked chests[/b], in any base, at any crafting station or NPC, as if the materials were in that base's chests.
[*][b]Dyes from your linked chests[/b] at the coloring station.
[*][b]Use the repair kit[/b] from the window, like other consumables.
[*][b]Favorite borders that stay behind the game's item menu[/b] (RMB on an item). Right now the gold border is drawn on top of that menu.
[/list]

